concept expressions {
  name     = "Expressions"
  summary  = "The expression grammar — operators, member access, calls, and constructor forms."
  related  = [numbers, strings, control_flow, functions]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "Every field value, function argument, and `let` right-hand side is an **expression** — something that produces a value. WCL's expression grammar is small: literals, identifiers, member access, calls, operators, and a handful of constructor forms."
    callout "Covered elsewhere" { class = ["info"]  body = "Literal forms live with their types (Numbers, Strings, Booleans, Symbols, Optionals, Lists, Tensors). Function literals are in Functions; if / match / let / block in Control Flow." }
    h2 "Operators"
    table {
      header = ["Group", "Operators"]
      rows = [
        ["Arithmetic", "`+` `-` `*` `/` `%`"],
        ["Comparison", "`==` `!=` `<` `<=` `>` `>=`"],
        ["Logical", "`&&` `||` `!`"],
        ["Coalescing", "`??` (left value unless `none`)"],
        ["Unary", "`-expr` (negate), `!expr` (not)"],
      ]
    }
    p "Precedence follows the usual conventions: unary tightest, then `*` `/` `%`, then `+` `-`, then comparison, then `&&`, then `||`, then `??` loosest. Use parentheses to group when in doubt."
    h2 "Numeric promotion"
    p "Arithmetic and comparison widen mixed [numeric](concept_numbers) operands to a common type, so cross-width and integer/float mixing work without explicit casts."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
a = 1 + 2.0        // i64 widened to f64 -> 3.0
b = 1u32 == 1i64   // true
c = 3.0 * 2u8      // 6.0
SRC
    }
    h2 "Member access"
    p "A dotted path reads a field. Access chains through records, variant payloads, and any composite that exposes named members."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
region = service.metadata.region
deep   = config.services.web.metadata.region
SRC
    }
    h2 "Function calls"
    p "Parentheses call a function or constructor. Arguments are expressions, evaluated lazily; the call evaluates the body in a fresh context."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
n      = len(items)
total  = sum(map(items, fn(x: i64) -> i64 x * 2))
shape  = Point { x: 1.0, y: 2.0 }
SRC
    }
    h2 "Variant construction"
    p "Build a union variant with `Union::Variant`. Record bodies go in braces, typeref payloads in parentheses, unit constructors stand bare. See [Unions](concept_unions)."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
a = Shape::Circle { radius: 5.0, stroke: 0.5 }
b = Shape::Polygon(7)
c = Shape::Empty
SRC
    }
    h2 "List literals"
    p "Square brackets and commas build a `list<T>`. See [Lists](concept_lists) for nested lists and the collection builtins."
    code "wcl" { source = <<'SRC'
xs    = [1, 2, 3]
names = ["alice", "bob"]
empty = []
SRC
    }
  }
}
